Now ApiDtos: 
- SegmentInput add `Boolean plural` (nullable → plain).
- AddSegmentRequest add `Boolean plural`.
- New DTOs: PluralCategoryInput(category, content), SubmitPluralTranslationsRequest(requestId, sourceVersion, categories) with sorted canonical constructor, ApprovePluralCategoryRequest(requestId, category, translationVersion), PluralSubmitResponse, PluralApprovalResponse.

For canonicalization: SubmitPluralTranslationsRequest compact constructor sorts categories by category name. Records with compact constructor: 

```java
public record SubmitPluralTranslationsRequest(..., List<@Valid PluralCategoryInput> categories) {
    public SubmitPluralTranslationsRequest {
        if (categories != null) {
            categories = categories.stream()
                    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(PluralCategoryInput::category))
                    .toList();
        }
    }
}
```

Wait — sorting with null category would NPE; validation handles @NotBlank later but constructor runs before validation. Use Comparator.comparing with nullsFirst. Category could be null → use `Comparator.comparing(PluralCategoryInput::category, Comparator.nullsFirst(Comparator.naturalOrder()))`.

Also "换序视为同参" — since the hash serializes the request object after construction, sorted list gives canonical hash. 

Responses:
- PluralCategoryVersionView(String category, int translationVersion)
- PluralSubmitResponse(long documentId, String segmentId, String language, int sourceVersion, int termVersion, int draftVersion, List<PluralCategoryVersionView> categories)
- PluralApprovalResponse(long documentId, String segmentId, String language, String category, String reviewer, int translationVersion, int sourceVersion)

Also update SegmentInput/AddSegmentRequest javadoc. Note: adding a component to SegmentInput record — JSON without "plural" → null. Good.

